{"id":"000W66","title":"Chaosomino","author":"Prof.Dori","solvedCount":1,"difficulty":4,"rating":"N/A","firstSeen":"2026-11-22T16:21:09+00:00","posted":"Heute, 11:31 Uhr","rules":"Chaosomino\n\nI and aqjhs did collaborate to make this puzzle for an event where we didn't knew who we were collabing with. Hope you enjoy it.\n\nRules:\n\nThe puzzle has two 6x6 grids, one is Chaos Construction while the other is Fillomino.\n\nChaos Construction: Divide the grid into six orthogonally-connected regions, each containing six cells. Each row, column and region must contain the numbers 1 to 6, once each.\n\nFillomino: Divide the grid into regions of orthogonally connected cells. Each cell should contain a number equal to the size of its region (i.e. the number of cells in its region). Regions of same size can't touch each other orthogonally.\n\nOuter clues are both X-Sums and Region Counters.\n\nX-Sums: Clues outside the grid give the sum of any numbers in the first X cells from the direction of the clue, where X is the first digit in that direction.\n\nRegion Counters: Clues outside the grid give the number of different regions seen across both grids.\n\nRegion borders: Thick black lines are region borders.\n\nQuestion Marks: A '?' is a positive integer between 1-9. A '??' is a positive integer between 10-99.\n\nClick here to start the puzzle","solutionCode":"Row 4 with dashes between borders (for example 1-23-456-77-88-99).","tags":["Sudoku","Fillomino","X-Sums (Variante)","Chaos Construction (Variante)"],"links":[{"url":"https://sudokupad.app/7qpy4jp3p2","kind":"sudokupad"}],"data":"","error":null,"settings":{},"link":"https://sudokupad.app/7qpy4jp3p2","linkKind":"sudokupad","summary":{"format":"scl","decoded":true,"rows":8,"cols":14,"cages":0,"hasSolution":true,"features":["lines","underlays"]},"attempts":0,"fetched":"2026-11-22T16:21:09+00:00"}